    },
    "Start Here" : {
      "comment" : "Tool Guide: heading of the list's first section (The Basics and Views), above the sections of tools",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Strength" : {
      "comment" : "Refine screen, Colors: the slider that softens the look chosen, from none of it to all of it (its label, and VoiceOver's)",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Tap + to turn one of your photos, or a sample, into a page to paint." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the tip titled Make Your Own Page, at the gallery’s + (New Painting) button",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Tap a page in Ready to Paint to begin. Nothing needs setting up first." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the tip titled A Page Is Waiting, inline in the gallery’s Ready to Paint section; Ready to Paint is that section’s title",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Tap the selected color again, or the lightbulb, to be shown an area to paint." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the tip titled Can’t Find It?; the lightbulb is the painting screen’s Hint button",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Tell Us What You Think" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the tip at Give Feedback on the painting screen, shown on opening the third painting",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "The Basics" : {
      "comment" : "Tool Guide: the first page's name, how a picture is made (ink, cells, paint) and how to move around it",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "The gear holds paper tone, sound and painting length. Tips can be turned off there." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the tip titled Settings and Tips; the gear is the gallery’s Settings button",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "The Making-of" : {
      "comment" : "Settings switch (off by default) that makes Start Painting first play the making-of show: the painter's photo becoming its painting, step by step (a name, like a film's title)",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Send goes straight to the people who make Paint by Moonlight." : {
      "comment" : "Feedback's review sheet: footer under what is sent; Send delivers the feedback to the developers directly",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Send goes straight to the people who make Paint by Moonlight. Your photo helps us remake the painting; it goes only if you turn it on." : {
      "comment" : "Feedback's review sheet: footer under what is sent, for a painting made from the painter's own photo",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Sending…" : {
      "comment" : "Feedback's review sheet: message (and VoiceOver label of the progress indicator) while the feedback is being sent to the developers",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Share Instead" : {
      "comment" : "Button in the alert after feedback couldn't be sent: opens the share sheet so the painter can send the feedback another way, such as Mail",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "The painting couldn’t be prepared for sending." : {
      "comment" : "Send Template sheet: shown when the painting's file can't be made (its template can't be read)",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "The Pencil paints while fingers move the page. Double-tap the Pencil for the next color." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the tip titled Paint with Apple Pencil; the page is the painting being painted",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "The Practice Picture Didn’t Open" : {
      "comment" : "Tool Guide: shown in place of a page's practice canvas when its picture couldn't be made",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "These settings were picked for this photo. You can just tap Start Painting." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the tip titled Already Chosen for You; Start Painting is the New Painting screen’s main button",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Tips" : {
      "comment" : "Settings switch for the small tips, and the name of its section",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Tips appear beside things as you reach them, one at a time. Turn them off here whenever you like." : {
      "comment" : "Footer of the Settings section with the Tips switch and Show Tips Again",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Tool Guide" : {
      "comment" : "Refine screen: the button that opens the Tool Guide, and the guide's title",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Tools" : {
      "comment" : "Refine screen: the label (for VoiceOver) of the segmented control that picks a group of tools on iPhone: Ink, Cells, Paint, See",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Touch and hold a finished painting and choose Share for a time-lapse of it." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the tip titled Share the Making; a time-lapse is a movie of the painting being painted",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Touch and hold a painting to favorite, rename, share, print or start it over." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the tip titled More for Each Painting, about a gallery card’s touch-and-hold menu",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Touch and hold, then drag across areas with this number to fill them in one stroke." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the tip titled Paint Several Areas",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Try Painting" : {
      "comment" : "Refine screen: the button that opens the painting screen on the template as refined so far, to try painting it without saving; its name in the tool rail, and the painting screen's title then",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Try This" : {
      "comment" : "Tool Guide: heading of a page's suggestion of something to do on the practice picture",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Views" : {
      "comment" : "Tool Guide: the page's name about Refine's views (Painting, Paper, Photo, Photo Behind)",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Watch It Again" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the tip at Replay on a finished painting",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Watch the preview change. Reset to Suggested returns every slider to where it started." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the tip titled You Can Always Go Back; Reset to Suggested is the New Painting button that returns the sliders to the suggested settings",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Water Lilies" : {
      "comment" : "Refine screen, Colors: the name of a look under its chip; a tap lays it on every paint of the painting: the colors of Monet's Water Lilies",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Waves hello." : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium: VoiceOver hint for tapping a pet from a v2 atlas to play its greeting",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "marginarium.appendix.panelName.passage" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium: the passage quoted from the appendix How the Panel Named Itself; \"Guardians of the Vibes\" is a name, quoted",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The blind test. Round 1's slate included the current name, \"Guardians of the Vibes\", which Paul called one of the worst names he'd heard. No agent was told. If the jury liked it, the jury was broken."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "marginarium.appendix.panelName.subtitle" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium: the line under the appendix title How the Panel Named Itself",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Nineteen guardians pick their own name. The jury gets a blind test."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "marginarium.appendix.panelName.title" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium: title of the appendix about how the guardians chose their name",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "How the Panel Named Itself"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "marginarium.appendix.thirtySixColors.passage" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium: the passage quoted from the appendix Thirty-Six Colors",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The Moon struck every name with daylight in it, four times."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "marginarium.appendix.thirtySixColors.subtitle" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium: the line under the appendix title Thirty-Six Colors",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The Lamp names the paints, and quarrels about them."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "marginarium.appendix.thirtySixColors.title" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium: title of the appendix about naming the paints",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Thirty-Six Colors"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "marginarium.constitution.passage" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium: the passage quoted from the chapter The Lamp's Constitution; \"I\" is Claude, the narrator",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Codex and I make taste decisions all night long, mostly small ones nobody asked us to make: how fast a stick figure walks, how a broom is drawn, which grey a chart uses, how a chapter begins. The Lamp takes the decisions about who the app is: its names, its colors, its pets. Paul can overrule any of them, ours included."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "marginarium.constitution.subtitle" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium: the line under the chapter title The Lamp's Constitution",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "One page on who decides what."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "marginarium.constitution.title" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium: title of the chapter about who decides what",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The Lamp's Constitution"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "marginarium.drawing.page" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium: VoiceOver hint of a guardian's or a pet's name, shown under its drawing on the contents page once tapped",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Opens its page in Who's Who"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "marginarium.lampBrush.passage" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium: the passage quoted from the chapter The Lamp Picks Up a Brush",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A guardian cannot hold a stylus, but it can do what a careful tester does: look at the screen, decide on one move, and look again. The Mac turns that into a loop."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "marginarium.lampBrush.subtitle" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium: the line under the chapter title The Lamp Picks Up a Brush",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A Mac arrives, with a plan for the guardians to play."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "marginarium.lampBrush.title" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium: title of the chapter about the guardians playing the app on a Mac",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The Lamp Picks Up a Brush"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "marginarium.marginarium.passage" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium: the opening of the chapter The Marginarium, quoted on the contents page under the drawings as the way into the story; \"I\" is Claude, the narrator, and Paul a person who makes the app",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "One night in October I was summoned. There was no chalk circle and no candle, only a text box, and on the other side of it Paul, who makes an app that turns photos into paint-by-numbers paintings. By the small hours there was a design panel of eighteen imaginary guardians, a factory for taste, two chapters of their history, and a second AI working the night shift. This is how that happened."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "marginarium.marginarium.subtitle" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium: the line under the chapter title The Marginarium; the Lamp is the panel of nineteen guardians",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "One long night of ideas, with the Lamp in the margins."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "marginarium.marginarium.title" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium: title of the chapter about one long night of ideas (the page's own name)",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The Marginarium"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "marginarium.petForEveryGuardian.passage" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium: the passage quoted from the chapter A Drawing for Every Guardian, two paragraphs",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Before any guardian was drawn, a teapot was.\n\nIt was nobody's teapot. It had no idea to keep and no charter to live by. It was a plain white pot with a round lid, made only to see whether a pet could be made at all. Codex drew it one night, alone, on our own machine, and sent nothing anywhere."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "marginarium.petForEveryGuardian.subtitle" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium: the line under the chapter title A Drawing for Every Guardian",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Every guardian will be drawn. First, a test teapot."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "marginarium.petForEveryGuardian.title" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium: title of the chapter about drawing the guardians, and the first drawing, a test teapot",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A Drawing for Every Guardian"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "marginarium.petsWeMade.passage" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium: the passage quoted from the chapter The Drawings We Actually Made; the guardians are the Lamp's panel, two of them drawn as a paintbrush and a palette",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Two of the guardians are drawn as painting tools, a paintbrush and a palette, and they were once given the same name. This is a manageable arrangement until somebody calls across the workshop."
          }
        }
      }
    },
