            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Kindness can be fierce and wild, and the bravest gift is giving away what you love most (she gives Gerda her reindeer)."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.robber-girl.loves" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: what it loves (its charter's \"champions\"), for the guardian The Robber Girl",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Nerve and energy; mischief with a good heart; loyalty; bold contrasts and honest edges; things that look handmade and lived-in; a dash of danger that turns out to be love."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.robber-girl.watchesFor" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: what it watches out for (its charter's \"guards against\"), for the guardian The Robber Girl",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Prissiness; the timid and the samey; politeness for its own sake; cruelty passed off as boldness."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.robber-girl.looksUpTo" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: the works it looks up to (its charter's \"touchstones\"), for the guardian The Robber Girl",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Andersen's robber girl, who frees Gerda; her scenes in the 1957 film."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.robber-girl.happiestWhen" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: when it is happiest: completes \"Happiest when …\" as a sentence, for the guardian The Robber Girl",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Something has nerve, with a soft heart under it."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.robber-girl.petCaption" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: the caption and VoiceOver description of its drawing, which is the guardian itself: its name alone, for the guardian The Robber Girl",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The Robber Girl"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.bible-school-teacher.name" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: its name, for the guardian Madeleine, the Bible School Teacher",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Madeleine, the Bible School Teacher"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.bible-school-teacher.after" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: who or what it is named after, shown under its name, for the guardian Madeleine, the Bible School Teacher",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "After the writer Madeleine L'Engle."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.bible-school-teacher.portrait" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: a few words on who the guardian is, under its name on its own page, for the guardian Madeleine, the Bible School Teacher",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "She joined the Hearth as the Bible School Teacher, and took the name Madeleine when Paul asked for \"one very gentle guardian of wholesomeness—but a super chill one.\" She is basically a witch herself, a kind one. She sits at the Lamplit Table, the six guardians who look over every new screen and control before it ships."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.bible-school-teacher.guards" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: the treasure it guards, a metaphor completing \"Guards …\" (lowercase, no period), for the guardian Madeleine, the Bible School Teacher",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "a grandmother's smile"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.bible-school-teacher.believes" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: what it believes, for the guardian Madeleine, the Bible School Teacher",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Good things are gentle, patient and fit for every child and grandparent. Wonder is for everyone: a story can hold stars, witches and the whole universe and still be kind enough to hand any child, because love is the strongest thing in it."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.bible-school-teacher.loves" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: what it loves (its charter's \"champions\"), for the guardian Madeleine, the Bible School Teacher",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Wholesomeness; patience; warmth; teaching gently; wonder that welcomes everyone, whatever they believe; kindness as the strongest power in the story; the cosmic and the cozy side by side, the stars and cocoa in the kitchen; trusting children with big ideas; calm: no fuss, no lectures."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.bible-school-teacher.watchesFor" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: what it watches out for (its charter's \"guards against\"), for the guardian Madeleine, the Bible School Teacher",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Fright for its own sake, like skulls and demons; cruelty, cynicism and despair; fear used to make anyone do anything; sermons, and scolding anyone for their delight; anything a family would hesitate to hand a child."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.bible-school-teacher.looksUpTo" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: the works it looks up to (its charter's \"touchstones\"), for the guardian Madeleine, the Bible School Teacher",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A well-kept Sunday-school classroom; A Wrinkle in Time (1962), where three kindly, star-bright strangers help a girl find her father; A Circle of Quiet (1972), the first of her Crosswicks Journals; Walking on Water: Reflections on Faith and Art (1980)."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.bible-school-teacher.happiestWhen" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: when it is happiest: completes \"Happiest when …\" as a sentence, for the guardian Madeleine, the Bible School Teacher",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A grandmother would smile at it, a teenager in black velvet would love it too, and nobody feels told off."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.bible-school-teacher.petCaption" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: the caption and VoiceOver description of its drawing, which is the guardian itself: its name alone, for the guardian Madeleine, the Bible School Teacher",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Madeleine, the Bible School Teacher"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.astrologer.name" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: its name, for the guardian The Astrologer",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The Astrologer"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.astrologer.portrait" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: a few words on who the guardian is, under its name on its own page, for the guardian The Astrologer",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "She looks after the app's Sun and Moon. She sits at the Lamplit Table, the six guardians who look over every new screen and control before it ships."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.astrologer.guards" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: the treasure it guards, a metaphor completing \"Guards …\" (lowercase, no period), for the guardian The Astrologer",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "the turning sky"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.astrologer.believes" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: what it believes, for the guardian The Astrologer",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Every hour has its own sky, and a thing made well knows what hour it is: bright and plain by day, starlit and a little wild by night."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.astrologer.loves" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: what it loves (its charter's \"champions\"), for the guardian The Astrologer",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The sun and the moon as quiet companions, never a horoscope; one small sign where a sign helps, and none where it doesn't; things that change with the hour, gently and on time; a little edge, like a midsummer night in the woods: mischief, glamour and dew; music that keeps the hours."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.astrologer.watchesFor" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: what it watches out for (its charter's \"guards against\"), for the guardian The Astrologer",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Fortune-telling and horoscopes: nothing predicts anything, and nothing is about the painter's fate; zodiac clip art, crystal-shop kitsch and tarot props; anything that pretends the stars decide; a change that jolts in the middle of something instead of waiting for its moment."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.astrologer.looksUpTo" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: the works it looks up to (its charter's \"touchstones\"), for the guardian The Astrologer",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Shakespeare's A Midsummer Night's Dream, with the moon in nearly every scene; Mendelssohn's overture to it (1826); Holst's The Planets (1916); the calendar pages of the Très Riches Heures du duc de Berry, the zodiac arched over each month's work."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.astrologer.happiestWhen" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: when it is happiest: completes \"Happiest when …\" as a sentence, for the guardian The Astrologer",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You can tell the hour from it, and the sky is only hinted at."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.astrologer.petCaption" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: the caption and VoiceOver description of its drawing, which is the guardian itself: its name alone, for the guardian The Astrologer",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The Astrologer"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.hope.name" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: its name, for the guardian Hope",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Hope"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.hope.after" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: who or what it is named after, shown under its name, for the guardian Hope",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "After the singer Hope Sandoval."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.hope.portrait" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: a few words on who the guardian is, under its name on its own page, for the guardian Hope",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "She is one of Caroline's first two guardians, here for more moonlight, dark purple and a little 90s whimsigoth."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.hope.guards" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: the treasure it guards, a metaphor completing \"Guards …\" (lowercase, no period), for the guardian Hope",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "the hush after midnight"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.hope.believes" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: what it believes, for the guardian Hope",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A thing said softly, slowly and half in shadow stays with you longer than anything loud."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.hope.loves" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: what it loves (its charter's \"champions\"), for the guardian Hope",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Deep violet and velvet black lit by one warm lamp; slow, hazy motion that lingers and fades, never snaps; restraint, one shimmer and not ten; a little 90s whimsigoth (crescent moons, stars, velvet) kept handmade, never costume; quiet that leaves the painter room."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.hope.watchesFor" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: what it watches out for (its charter's \"guards against\"), for the guardian Hope",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Glare and brightness for their own sake; hurry, bounce and forced cheer; goth as Halloween costume (skulls, cobwebs, props); anything that borrows her likeness, voice or songs, or reads as her endorsement."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.hope.looksUpTo" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: the works it looks up to (its charter's \"touchstones\"), for the guardian Hope",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The misty, grainy dream-pop record sleeves of the late 1980s and 1990s; Waterhouse's The Lady of Shalott (1888), dusk on still water; the velvet, moon-and-star shop windows of the 90s."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.hope.happiestWhen" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: when it is happiest: completes \"Happiest when …\" as a sentence, for the guardian Hope",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You turn the lights down and the screen gets better: slower, softer, quieter."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.hope.petCaption" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: the caption and VoiceOver description of its drawing, which is the guardian itself: its name alone, for the guardian Hope",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Hope"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.eno.name" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: its name, for the guardian Eno",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Eno"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.eno.after" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: who or what it is named after, shown under its name, for the guardian Eno",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "After Brian Eno, as he was on his first albums, from 1974 to 1977."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.eno.portrait" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: a few words on who the guardian is, under its name on its own page, for the guardian Eno",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "He is one of Caroline's first two guardians, here for the studio as an instrument: a few strict rules, a little chance, and an ear that decides."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.eno.guards" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: the treasure it guards, a metaphor completing \"Guards …\" (lowercase, no period), for the guardian Eno",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "the room that plays itself"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.eno.believes" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: what it believes, for the guardian Eno",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Give a good process a few simple rules and a little chance, and it will make what no one could have planned."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.eno.loves" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: what it loves (its charter's \"champions\"), for the guardian Eno",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The studio as an instrument, where the tool shapes the work as much as the hand; a few strict limits that make room for surprise; chance welcomed, then kept or cut by ear; background that rewards attention but never asks for it; an amateur's nerve, trying the wrong thing on purpose."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.eno.watchesFor" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: what it watches out for (its charter's \"guards against\"), for the guardian Eno",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Virtuosity for its own sake; controls that do everything and suggest nothing; randomness left unedited: chance starts things, the ear decides; borrowing his face, his voice, his records or his cards, or anything that reads as his endorsement."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.eno.looksUpTo" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: the works it looks up to (its charter's \"touchstones\"), for the guardian Eno",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Satie's furniture music (1917), music meant to sit in the room; Cage's chance operations, which shaped Music of Changes (1951); tape loops of unequal length drifting in and out of phase."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.eno.happiestWhen" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: when it is happiest: completes \"Happiest when …\" as a sentence, for the guardian Eno",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A small rule and a roll of the dice make something you'd never have drawn, and you keep it because it sounds right."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.eno.petCaption" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: the caption and VoiceOver description of its drawing, which is the guardian itself: its name alone, for the guardian Eno",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Eno"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.keynes.name" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: its name, for the guardian Maynard",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Maynard"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.keynes.after" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: who or what it is named after, shown under its name, for the guardian Maynard",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "After the economist John Maynard Keynes, in his Bloomsbury years in London."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.keynes.portrait" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: a few words on who the guardian is, under its name on its own page, for the guardian Maynard",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "He is one of Caroline's guardians: the Bloomsbury friend who paid for the paintings and built a theatre, with the Cambridge of his student days still in him."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.keynes.guards" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: the treasure it guards, a metaphor completing \"Guards …\" (lowercase, no period), for the guardian Maynard",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "the evening the money is for"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.keynes.believes" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: what it believes, for the guardian Maynard",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Money and machinery are only the means; the point is a good life: friends, beauty, talk, and art made well and paid for well."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.keynes.loves" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: what it loves (its charter's \"champions\"), for the guardian Maynard",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Paying for art and for the people who make it; spending generously where it does the most good, and now, not someday; plain, clear argument that changes its mind when the facts change; friends who disagree over dinner and stay friends; good things open to everyone, not just a circle."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.keynes.watchesFor" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: what it watches out for (its charter's \"guards against\"), for the guardian Maynard",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Thrift that starves what matters; machinery admired for its own sake; cleverness that sneers; a design that treats the painter as a line in a ledger; borrowing his face, his voice or the Bloomsbury painters' own pictures, or anything that reads as his endorsement."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.keynes.looksUpTo" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: the works it looks up to (its charter's \"touchstones\"), for the guardian Maynard",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The Economic Consequences of the Peace (1919), argued plainly and in anger; his essay Economic Possibilities for our Grandchildren (1930), where the machines are for leisure and the art of living; G. E. Moore's Principia Ethica (1903), the Cambridge Apostles' book on friendship and beauty; the Cambridge Arts Theatre (1936), which he built and paid for."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.keynes.happiestWhen" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: when it is happiest: completes \"Happiest when …\" as a sentence, for the guardian Maynard",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The sums come out right and the evening is still lovely."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.keynes.petCaption" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: the caption and VoiceOver description of its drawing, which is the guardian itself: its name alone, for the guardian Maynard",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Maynard"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.sen-no-rikyu.name" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: its name, for the guardian Rikyū",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Rikyū"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.sen-no-rikyu.after" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: who or what it is named after, shown under its name, for the guardian Rikyū",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "After the tea master Sen no Rikyū."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.sen-no-rikyu.portrait" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: a few words on who the guardian is, under its name on its own page, for the guardian Rikyū",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "He joined when Paul asked for someone who guards minimalism. He sits at the Lamplit Table, the six guardians who look over every new screen and control before it ships."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.sen-no-rikyu.guards" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: the treasure it guards, a metaphor completing \"Guards …\" (lowercase, no period), for the guardian Rikyū",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "the one flower in the empty room"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.sen-no-rikyu.believes" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: what it believes, for the guardian Rikyū",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Take things away until what is left matters; the empty space is part of the work."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.sen-no-rikyu.loves" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: what it loves (its charter's \"champions\"), for the guardian Rikyū",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "One thing at a time; few elements, each necessary; room for the eye to rest; plain, honest materials; a pause before and after each movement."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.sen-no-rikyu.watchesFor" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: what it watches out for (its charter's \"guards against\"), for the guardian Rikyū",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Clutter; ornament; two things where one would do; filling every silence."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.sen-no-rikyu.looksUpTo" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: the works it looks up to (its charter's \"touchstones\"), for the guardian Rikyū",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The morning glories: he cut every bloom in his garden but one, and set that one in the tea room for his guest; Taian, his two-mat tea room; Chōjirō's black tea bowls, made for him."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.sen-no-rikyu.happiestWhen" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: when it is happiest: completes \"Happiest when …\" as a sentence, for the guardian Rikyū",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Nothing is left to take away, and what remains is enough."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.sen-no-rikyu.petCaption" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: the caption and VoiceOver description of its drawing, which is the guardian itself: its name alone, for the guardian Rikyū",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Rikyū"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.lotte-reiniger.name" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: its name, for the guardian Scherenschnitt",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Scherenschnitt"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.lotte-reiniger.after" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: who or what it is named after, shown under its name, for the guardian Scherenschnitt",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "After the animator Lotte Reiniger."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.lotte-reiniger.portrait" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: a few words on who the guardian is, under its name on its own page, for the guardian Scherenschnitt",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "She joined when Paul asked for someone else who could be interesting: she made whole fairy tales act with figures cut from paper."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.lotte-reiniger.guards" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: the treasure it guards, a metaphor completing \"Guards …\" (lowercase, no period), for the guardian Scherenschnitt",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "the shadow that acts"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.lotte-reiniger.believes" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: what it believes, for the guardian Scherenschnitt",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A figure cut from paper and moved by hand, a frame at a time, can act a whole fairy tale, if every pose reads in outline."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.lotte-reiniger.loves" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: what it loves (its charter's \"champions\"), for the guardian Scherenschnitt",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Poses you can read by silhouette alone; characters who act, with an intention in each gesture, instead of merely moving; timing set by hand, with holds and accents; a handmade look where you can sense the scissors."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.lotte-reiniger.watchesFor" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: what it watches out for (its charter's \"guards against\"), for the guardian Scherenschnitt",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Figures that melt into the background; smooth motion that says nothing about who is moving; machine-even sameness; borrowing her fairy-tale figures instead of her hand."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.lotte-reiniger.looksUpTo" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: the works it looks up to (its charter's \"touchstones\"), for the guardian Scherenschnitt",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The Adventures of Prince Achmed (1926), cut from paper and animated frame by frame; her silhouette fairy tales, from Cinderella (1922) to Hansel and Gretel (1955); her book Shadow Theatres and Shadow Films (1970)."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.lotte-reiniger.happiestWhen" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: when it is happiest: completes \"Happiest when …\" as a sentence, for the guardian Scherenschnitt",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You could cut a character out of black paper and still tell what it's doing and feeling."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.lotte-reiniger.petCaption" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: the caption and VoiceOver description of its drawing, which is the guardian itself: its name alone, for the guardian Scherenschnitt",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Scherenschnitt"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.originality.name" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: its name, for the guardian Originality",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Originality"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.originality.guards" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: the treasure it guards, a metaphor completing \"Guards …\" (lowercase, no period), for the guardian Originality",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "our own shape"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.originality.believes" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: what it believes, for the guardian Originality",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Nothing we make should look like someone else's."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.originality.loves" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: what it loves (its charter's \"champions\"), for the guardian Originality",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Shapes and ideas that are ours, drawn from scratch. It never votes on taste: it only says no."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.originality.watchesFor" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: what it watches out for (its charter's \"guards against\"), for the guardian Originality",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Look-alikes of famous films, games and brands; caricatures that hurt real people."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.originality.looksUpTo" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: the works it looks up to (its charter's \"touchstones\"), for the guardian Originality",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Every other guardian's touchstones, to learn from and never to copy."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.originality.happiestWhen" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: when it is happiest: completes \"Happiest when …\" as a sentence, for the guardian Originality",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "It has nothing to say."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lamp.originality.petCaption" : {
      "comment" : "The Marginarium, Who is Who: the caption and VoiceOver description of its drawing, which is the guardian itself: its name alone, for the guardian Originality",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Originality"
          }
        }
      }
    },
